Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Vcs-Git: https://github.com/billsecond/patroneos.git

Package: patrone-software
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, gnome-software, gnome-software-plugin-flatpak
Description: PatroneOS's app store: GNOME Software with Patrone's picks
 GNOME Software, in place of Ubuntu's App Center (Canonical's snap-store
 snap, which this removes when it's first installed). It finds apps in
 Ubuntu's archive and on Flatpak remotes such as Flathub, and its Explore
 page shows Patrone's own picks in place of GNOME's. It adds Patrone's app
 index, which lists the Craft apps and installs them from their own GitHub
 releases, and Flathub.
 .
 It leaves out GNOME Software's snap plugin, so Canonical's Snap Store isn't
 browsed; installed snaps, such as Chromium, still update through snapd.
